# GDScript conventions

## Avoid brittle `res://` paths

- Prefer `class_name` for shared scripts — call by type, no `preload("res://...")`
- Prefer `@export` / `@export_file` / PackedScene refs set in the editor (survive moves via UID)
- Prefer relative `preload("sibling.gd")` only when files must stay colocated
- Hardcoded `res://...` strings break on rename/move — avoid in app code; OK only for rare path maps (e.g. HFSM scene id → `.tscn`) until replaced by exports

## Naming

- Signals: `ev_*` (`ev_start_game`, `ev_correct_answer`)
- Files: `snake_case.gd`; scene colocated (`foo.gd` + `foo.tscn`)
- Types: `PascalCase` + `class_name` when shared
- FSM state IDs: `static func get_state() -> String`

## Patterns

- Wire dependencies with `@export` / `@export_category` (editor-first)
- UI / components / isolation: `godot-paradigm.md`
- Signal subscriptions → `EventListener`; `deinit()` in `_exit_tree` / `deinit`
- Apply config copies with `ResourceUtils.update_resource()` (same script required)
- Spawn: `PackedScene.instantiate()`; answers often `call_deferred("add_child", ...)`
- Extensible entities: component arrays + nested classes (see `AirPlane`, `Player`); components signal up, parent calls down

## Must

- Prefix new cross-object signals with `ev_`
- Tear down listeners on context/FSM leave
- Use existing physics layers: player=1, shots=2, answers=3
- Use InputMap actions (`shoot`, movement) — support touch + keyboard/mouse (Mobile, Steam, HTML)
- New controls/UI must be usable on phone landscape, desktop, and web

## Layers

- Feature code stays inside `src/features/{name}/`; expose signals/`initialize`, not cross-feature internals
- `core/` code must not reference `src/` or Quizmatik types
- Contexts orchestrate; they don't absorb feature implementation

## Avoid

- Autoloads for new game flow (use `RootEvents` / `GameEvents` Resources)
- Direct references across contexts
- Feature A importing Feature B internals (compose in context instead)
- Putting project-specific types into `core/`
- Desktop-only or touch-only features that break other target platforms
- New parallel FSM unless existing `core/lib/fsm` cannot fit
- Drive-by renames of typo filenames without explicit request
